In article <1993Jan5.112300.13993@wraxall.inmos.co.uk>, des@inmos.co.uk (David Shepherd) writes:
>Peter Snelling (snelling@bnr.ca) wrote:
>: I've just made a change to the identify scroll/spell feature to
>: make it easier to select the items you want to identify.
>
>: For instance, if you have two wands with inventory letters a and b, 
>: and you really want to identify b, but might also like to identify a,
>: it is currently not possible to first identify b, then (if you can
>: identify more items) identify a.
>
>i thought you could do this ... when it asks for what type of thing
>you want to identify just type // and this will go through the wands,
>alloweing you to id b then, assuming its a blessed scroll, continue
>through the rest before going through them all for a second time when you
>can id a.

When you type in a list of items, any duplicate items are removed.
So typing // or /="/ will only go through your wands once.

>: This change allow you to identify a set of items, and then if you
